  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I lifted up mine eyes again, and looked, and behold a man with a measuring line in his hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Then said I, Whither goest thou? And he said unto me, To measure Jerusalem, to see what is the breadth thereof, and what is the length thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And, behold, the angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And said unto him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Jerusalem shall be inhabited as towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle therein:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For I, saith the LORD, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Ho, ho, come forth, and flee from the land of the north, saith the LORD: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, saith the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Deliver thyself, O Zion, that dwellest with the daughter of Babylon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For thus saith the LORD of hosts; After the glory hath he sent me unto the nations which spoiled you: for he that toucheth you toucheth the apple of his eye.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For, behold, I will shake mine hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants: and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And many nations shall be joined to the LORD in that day, and shall be my people: and I will dwell in the midst of thee, and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And the LORD shall inherit Judah his portion in the holy land, and shall choose Jerusalem again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:zechariah:2:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD: for he is raised up out of his holy habitation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Zechariah 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:zechariah:2:13"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
